		(uuid "238c5fe0-ad9d-526b-88ab-1a4ba2accb72")
	)
	(text "1. POWER. The fused cigarette plug P1 (fuse value unknown) is the panel's only\n    power input. Its own lead is the two-wire cable W1 (brown = +, blue = -), which\n    enters under the deck at the notch corner. The drawing connects P1 to the\n    car outlet; its behavior with the car switched off needs checking.\n2. J+ AND J-. Under the deck everything joins at two points: J+ (on the USB\n    socket's + tab) and J- (on the 12 V socket's shell tab). The red and black\n    branches split off in heat-shrunk joints beside the socket plate (3502).\n3. SOCKETS. The USB socket X1 and the 12 V socket X2 are wired straight across\n    J+ and J-, so they work whenever the car outlet is live.\n4. WIRELESS CHARGER. The Qi pad U2 gets 12 V through a small two-pin plug J2.\n5. LIGHTS. Press SW1: it latches down and keeps the RGB lights on after release.\n    The drawing assumes SW1 interrupts the + feed to controller U1. U1 drives\n    three RGB LED heads through the in-line plugs J3. A phone app sets the colours.\n6. FIBRES. Heads H1 and H2 sit under the deck at the rear corners and shine into\n    side-glow fibres FO1 and FO2, which run along the top of the two side arms.\n    Head H3 has no fibre and lies loose in the car's tray by the gear lever.\n7. CLOCK. It has its own battery and no wires.\n8. CURRENT AT 12 V (approx.): USB up to 4-4.5 A, Qi pad 1.5-2 A, lights 0.5-1 A.\n    About 7 A in total, before anything is plugged into the 12 V socket X2.\n9. PROTECTION. Only the fuse in the plug tip and the car's own outlet fuse."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 12.7 178.435 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.7 1.7)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "744a7e0a-a777-5691-969b-b1ad4ba5ca1b")
	)
	(text "CONNECTIONS AND RATINGS TO VERIFY"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
